Package: radioberry
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 radioberry-dkms (= ${source:Version}),
 systemd,
 udev,
Description: RadioBerry 2.x HF transceiver on the Raspberry Pi 4 or 5
 radioberryd serves a RadioBerry 2.x HAT to SDR clients over openHPSDR
 Protocol 1 (Hermes-Lite 2 dialect) and Protocol 2, as
 radioberry.service. Transmit and the PA are off as installed; see
 /etc/radioberry/config.yaml.
 .
 Also included: the RadioBerry gateware (one image for the Raspberry Pi 5,
 one for the Pi 4, for the 10CL025 FPGA, built from source), the device
 tree overlay, and the tools rbprobe, rbcat, rbctl, p1probe and p2probe.
 The kernel driver is in radioberry-dkms.

Package: radioberry-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 dkms,
Recommends:
 linux-headers-rpi-v8 | linux-headers-rpi-2712,
Description: RadioBerry 2.x kernel driver (DKMS source)
 The radioberry.ko driver for the RadioBerry 2.x on the Raspberry Pi 4
 or 5: loads the gateware, streams receive and transmit over I2S (Pi 4)
 or the RP1 PIO (Pi 5), and gives userspace /dev/radioberry. DKMS builds it for each installed
 kernel and rebuilds it when the kernel is updated.

Package: radioberry-dev
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: RadioBerry 2.x driver ABI header
 radioberry_ioctl.h: the /dev/radioberry interface of the radioberry.ko
 driver, for programs that use the device directly.
